      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The Finnish defence ministry has imposed temporary airspace and maritime restrictions after a drone struck a Russian cargo vessel in international waters of the Gulf of Finland, causing a fire.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-21:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 21 November 2026, air alerts were raised in the Baltic Sea area by Finland and Estonia amid a Ukrainian drone attack.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387014408:96"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "In March and May 2026, several Ukrainian or suspected Ukrainian military drones entered NATO airspace, including Finland, after crossing from Russia during Ukrainian long-range attacks.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1387014408:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The events took place in the Gulf of Finland, the location given in the reports.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-21:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "According to Wikipedia's sources, side one lost 3 drones shot down, while side two lost 1 drone shot down.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1387014408:casualties-side-1-",
        "wiki:box:1387014408:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "The story was reported by AFP.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-21:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:00:58Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined it: “Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:c7c9c4110e34"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-21T00:01:04Z",
      "text": "DW headlined it: “Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace.”",
